      "textEn": "9. Similarly, the Mahiyasan Fadarji Abhishek - of the lotus feet of great men,\nis the one who bestows the welfare of the receiver, but the same dust can also cause loss. Those who commit offenses against the lotus feet of some\ngreat man, they wither, their divine qualities diminish. Great men can forgive crimes, but Krishna does not forgive the dust of the lotus feet of that great man.\nHe does not forgive the crime committed. Just as someone may tolerate the scorching sun on their head,\nbut cannot tolerate it with their feet. The criminal continuously falls down, therefore he commits offenses against the feet of the Mahatma.\nGenerally, they commit offenses that consider the unstable body as self.\nKing Daksha was extremely deluded because he considered the body as the soul. He committed an offense against the feet of Shivji, because he considered himself the father of Sati's body and considered his body\nsuperior to Shiva.\n\nTheir name, which has two letters, Shi and Va, is to purify man from all sins. Their\norders are never disregarded. Shiva is always pure, and besides you, no one else\nhates him.\nMeaning: Since among the beings of this physical world, Shiva is the greatest soul, therefore those who"
