      "textEn": "92\nThose who consider the body as the soul, for them, their name is supremely beneficial. If such people take refuge in Lord Shiva, then they will gradually understand that they are not the body, but the soul. ©. The meaning of Shiva is auspiciousness. The soul within is a blessing. Aham Brahmasmi ‘I am Brahman’ This is auspicious. Until someone\ndoes not identify with the soul, whatever they do is inauspicious. Of \"Shiva\"\nMeans \"'Mangalakari\" and devotees of Shiva slowly attain the state of self-realization, but this\nis not everything. A good life begins with self-realization. But there are some other duties as well. §—\nMan has to understand his relationship with God. If someone is truly a devotee of Shiva,\nthen he attains self-realization.\nBut if he is not quite intelligent, then he stops there and\nonly understands that he is the soul (Aham Brahmasmi). If he is intelligent, then he should keep moving forward on the path of Shiva, because Lord Shiva is constantly absorbed in the thoughts of Vasudeva. As it has been said before, ⏈— Satvam Vishuddham Vasudevashabditam - Lord Shiva always meditates on the lotus feet of Vasudeva Shri Krishna.\nIn this way, a person only realizes the auspicious position of Lord Shiva when\nhe worships Vishnu, because in the Shiv Purana, it is said of Shiva that the best worship\nis the worship of Vishnu. Lord Shiva is worshiped because he is the greatest devotee of Lord Vishnu ©. But\nWe should never make the mistake of considering Shiva and Vishnu on the same level. Doing so\nis an atheistic thought. In the Vaishnava Puranas, it is also said that Vishnu or Narayan is the most revered God.\nHe is, and he should not be compared to anyone, neither to Shiva nor to Brahma.\nOf other gods,\nThere is no question of it.\n\nThat which is greater than the feet of the feet,\nThat which is not spoken of, is the Brahmarasasavadhi.\nThat which is spoken of by the world, that which is the destruction of the wicked,\nThat which is spoken of by you, is the binding of the universe. 95 Shabdartham\nYat-pad-padmamu-- whose lotus feet; Mahatam-- of great men; Man-Alibhi-- from the minds of men; Nishevitam-- attached; Nishaevitam-- attached;\nStaying; Brahma-rasa-- of divine bliss (Brahma-rasa); Asava-Arthibhih-- in search of nectar; Lokasya-- of the common people; Yat--"
