      "textEn": "94\nKim va--or; Shiva-akhyam--calling Shiva; ashivam--inauspicious; na vidu--do not know; tvat-anye--other than you; brahma-adi--Brahma, etc.; tam--them (of Shiva); avakiry--scattered; jataha--with matted hair;\nimshane--in the cremation ground; tatu-malya-bhasma-no-kapal--those who wear garlands of skulls and apply ashes; avasat--remaining together;\npishachai--with demons; ye--those; murthabhi--from the head; dadhati--they wear; tatu-charan-avasrashtam--from their feet;\nfalling from the lotus feet..\nDo you think that even more respectable person than you, like Lord Brahma, this\nAmong the auspicious person known by the name of Shiva, do you not know? They live with demons in the cremation ground,\ntheir matted hair remains scattered over the body, they wear garlands of skulls, and the ashes of the cremation ground\nremain wrapped in the body, but even with these inauspicious qualities, a great man like Brahma\nrespectfully wears the flowers offered at his feet on his foreheads and honors them.\nMeaning: It is meaningless to criticize a great man like Shiva, and this is being said by his wife Sati, so that his superiority can be proven. First, he said, *'You call Shiva inauspicious,\nbecause he lives with demons in the cremation ground, applies the ashes of the dead to his body, and adorns himself with garlands of skulls.'\nYou have pointed out many of his faults; but you do not know that\nhis state is always divine. Although they appear inauspicious, then why do great men like Brahma\nrespect the dust of their lotus feet by wearing it on their heads, whom you\nrebuke?\"Since Sati was a virtuous woman and the wife of Shiva, it was her duty that\nshe establish Shiva's high position not only on emotions but also on facts. Shiva is no ordinary soul. That is what the scriptures say. They are neither at the level of God nor at the level of ordinary\nliving beings. Brahman is almost the common Jeevatma in all respects.\nSometimes when a\nordinary soul is not available, then the position of Brahma is taken by some expansion (part) of Vishnu\nis taken, but generally this position is taken by the most sacred soul of this universe. Thus, Shiva's position is always higher than Brahma in a legal sense, although Shivji was born as the son of Brahma. Here it is mentioned that even a man like Brahma accepts the so-called inauspicious dust and flowers at the lotus feet of Shiva. Among the nine great sages who are descendants of Brahma, Marichi,"
