      "textEn": "98\nHe delights in his own world, the great sage.\nAs is the path of gods and humans, separate,\nHe does not cast his own dharma upon others. 19. Meaning of the word\n\nNa- no; Veda- Veda-- the rules of the Vedas; Anuvartate-- follow; Mati-- mind; Swayam-- on one's own; Eva-- certainly;\nLoke-- in the world; Ramatah-- while enjoying; Maha-Muneh-- of the divine men; Yatha-- as; Gatih-- path, manner; Deva-\nManushyayah-- of humans and gods; Prithak- separate; Swayam- in oneself; Eva- alone; Dharme- duty; Na- not;\nParam-other; Kshipet- criticizes; Sthitah- while being situated..\nIt is better to fulfill one's duty than to criticize others. Great divine\nmen also sometimes violate the rules and regulations of the Vedas, because they do not need to follow\nthem, just as gods wander in the sky,\nbut ordinary people walk on the earth. Meaning: The conduct of the yogis and the most fallen bound soul seems the same.\nThe highest yogis can transgress all the rules of the Vedas, just as the gods who wander in the sky cross all the forests and rocks of the earth, but a common man has to face all these obstacles due to such\nlack of facility. Although the supremely beloved Shiva of the Vedas\ndoes not seem to follow even a trace of the rules, and such disobedience does not affect them\nnothing. But if a common man wants to imitate them, then he will make a great mistake. A common\nman should follow all the rituals of the Vedas, while a man who has attained a divine state\ndoes not need to follow all these. Daksha had accused Shiva that he does not follow the strict rituals of the Vedas,\nbut Sati forcefully wanted to say that she had no need to follow such\nrules. It is said that one who is as radiant as the sun or fire\ndoes not care about purity or impurity. Sunlight can sterilize an impure place\nIt is, but if someone else has to leave from there, then he will not remain without being affected. Man should not imitate Shiva, but should perform his assigned duties with diligence. He should not criticize a great man like Shivaji."
