      "textEn": "02\nNaten Dehen Hare Kritagaso\nDehodbhavenalamalam Kujanmana\nVriida Mamabhutkujanprasankhtas\nTajanma Dhigyo Mahatamavadyakrit. 22). Meaning of the word\nNa- not; Etena-- through this; Dehen-- by the body; Hare-- towards Shiva; Kruta- Agasah-- having committed an offense; Deha- Uddhave-- from your body;\nUpdra- Janana; Mama- mine; Abhut-\nwas; Ku-jan-prasankhatah-- with a bad person; Tat- Janma-- that birth; Dhik- Dikkara- disgraceful; Yah- who; Mahatam- of great men;\nAvadya- Krit- offender..\nYou are guilty of the lotus feet of Lord Shiva, and unfortunately, my body is born from you. I am feeling extremely ashamed of this physical relationship, and I am\nself-condemning that my body is contaminated by the relationship with such a person who is guilty of the lotus feet of a great man. Meaning: Shiva is the supreme among all the devotees of Lord Vishnu.\nIt is said-- Vaishnavana yathaa\nShambhuha / Shambhu means Shiva, the greatest devotee of Lord Vishnu ©. In the previous verses, Sati has said\nthat Shiva always remains in a divine state, because he remains in a pure Vasudeva state. Vasudev is that state, from which Vasudev Shri Krishna is born, therefore Shivji is the greatest devotee of Shri Krishna.\nAnd the conduct of Sati is ideal, because no one should tolerate the insult of Lord Vishnu or his devotee. Sati is not sorry to be Shiva's companion, but rather her sorrow is\nthat her body is born from Daksha, who is guilty of the lotus feet of Shiva. They consider themselves\nDhiktarati, because this body of theirs is given by their father Daksha. This line of lineage is yours, O Lord, with the bull.\nDakshayani, thus, when the mind is good.\nImmediately, with a smile, I will remove this obstacle.\nLooking at this, I will remove your obstacle. 23). Meaning of the word\nGotram--family relation; Tvadiya--yours; Bhagavan--lord of all gods; Vrishadhvaja--Shiva; Dakshayani--Daksha's\ndaughter, Dakshayani; Iti--in this way; Aah--says; Yada--when; Jana