      "textEn": "04\nResolved to sacrifice. Sati Yogeshwar Shiva's wife of | Shiva is the best among all yogis,\nbecause she knows all the yogic practices, therefore it seems that Sati also knows all this.\nEither she learned yoga from her husband, or because she is the daughter of a great emperor like Daksha, she\nis well-educated. The accomplishment of yoga lies in this that a person voluntarily leaves his body or gets rid of himself through the combination of material elements. Those yogis who attain perfection, their death does not occur according to natural\nrules, such accomplished yogis renounce their bodies according to their wishes. Generally,\na yogi first becomes accomplished by mastering the air within the body, and in this way, he brings the soul\nto the top of the brain.\nThen, when the flame erupts from the body, the Yogi can go anywhere according to his wish. In this type of yoga method, the soul is given recognition, and in this way, it is different from that\nso-called yoga method, which in the modern era has been extracted to control the cells of the body. In the real yoga method, the soul is adopted from one realm to another, or\nfrom one body to another, and this event suggests that\nSati wanted to transfer her soul to another body or realm.\nHaving made the Samanavilau victorious,\nRising from the Sodanamu and from the Nabhi Chakra.\nEfe Sthapya Dhiorasi Sthitam\nKanthadasharuvormadhyamaninditanayat. 25. Meaning of the word\nKrutva-- having established; Samanau-- in equilibrium; Anilau-- to the life and apana vayus; Jit-asana-- having subdued the asana; Sa- that (Sati); Udanam-- the life air; Uthapya-- having lifted up; Cha-- and; Nabhi-chakratah- on the navel chakra; 9: - Slowly\nSlowly; Hadi-- in the heart; Sthapya-- having established; Dhiya-- with intellect; Urasi-- towards the lung passage; Sthitam- having established; Kanthaat- through the throat; Yat: --Of the eyebrows; Madhyam--In the middle; Anindita-- Imperishable (Sati); Anayat-- Upward;\nTE\nFirst, he seated the asana as per the expected method, and then, by drawing the life force upwards, he established it in a balanced state near the navel. Then, by raising the life air,\nIntelligently, she took it into her heart, and then slowly, through the windpipe, gradually brought it between both eyebrows."
